From 179880a7635b3ac285f6eae8b7b738df622e72ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:35:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Multi-location Phase C (rebuilt): per-store KDS + terminals +
 walk-around QR
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rebuilt onto the current codebase (original patch no longer applied after this
week's Locations-tab work). Same behaviour:

- Per-store KDS: a store selector in the KDS top bar (multi-location only); the
  ticket feed is scoped to that store's Square location, so a Coffee Station at
  Mitchell and one at TulipTops each show only their own orders.
- Per-store card terminal: settings.pos.terminalByLocation maps each store to its
  own paired reader (falls back to the default reader for single-site). The POS
  resolves the reader for the current store; POS setup pairs/selects/disconnects
  for that store; /api/pos/order sends the checkout to the order store's reader.
  Includes a location-aware Disconnect button.
- Walk-around / general-order QR: Admin -> Locations generates a per-store QR
  encoding /?loc=<store> (no table) — scanning opens the app already set to that
  store, for ordering while walking the gardens. Download as PNG.

Verified headless: KDS selector lists both stores; POS resolves the right reader
per store (Front counter for a paired store, 'No terminal' for an unpaired one);
walk-around QR generates. Build + server checks pass.
